Development environment constraints

Do not modify platformio.ini, board configuration, upload settings, USB settings, serial-port settings, monitor settings, build flags, PlatformIO environments, CLion configuration, or device flashing/debugging behavior.

Do not attempt to connect to, monitor, reset, flash, upload to, or automatically test against the physical ESP32.

Do not create serial-port test harnesses or change USB CDC behavior.

You may compile the project with PlatformIO to check for compiler/linker errors, but stop after a successful compile. I will upload to the ESP32 and perform hardware testing manually.

Serial logging inside the game code is acceptable only when it is useful for debugging the feature, but do not change how the serial monitor itself is configured.

High: large monsters are only dirtied at their anchor when damage applies (combat.cpp). Replace that with markEntityFootprintDirty(*target) so a 2×2 spider fully redraws when hurt, killed, or marked with its red X.
•
High: combat is only partially map-generic. getMapEntities() supports forest and dungeon, but player lookup, combat detection, player targeting, and line of sight still directly use forest data (combat.cpp, combat.cpp, combat.cpp). A shared active-map accessor would make dungeon combat reliable and remove duplicate LOS code from monsterscripts.cpp.
•
High: gate Serial combat logging behind a debug macro. checkForCombat() logs every check and every nearby monster, which can noticeably stall input/rendering on hardware (combat.cpp). This is likely the best pure runtime optimization.
•
Medium: unify player and monster attack-resolution state. Combat has two parallel attack state systems (combat.h), with separate damage/timing paths. A single AttackResolution state would reduce duplicated logic and prevent future timing or redraw differences.
•
Medium: centralize turn completion. The monster action path advances turns directly, while nextTurn() does not explicitly handle the case where every combatant is invalid/dead. A finishCurrentTurn() helper and a “no live combatants” result would make the ranged-AI freeze fix more robust.
•
Low: reduce header coupling. combat.h includes monsterScripts.h, which includes combat.h back. Move implementation-only includes into .cpp files and remove the unused runCombatTurn() declaration (combat.h). This improves build times and maintainability, not frame rate.
I would keep the full redraw at combat start/end: it is needed to restore the map after opaque menus. The attack/target paths are already using dirty tiles appropriately apart from the large-target damage redraw above.
